MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The powered USB hub fits my purchases of USB adapters and a USB expansion card because it could help connect and power those peripherals; individual switches are useful, though ten ports may be excessive.",
    "The HDMI cable and USB hard drive relate to my practical computer accessory purchases, but that relevance alone does not give me a reason to buy either today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV and Echo devices do not address the computer connection needs behind my adapter and cable purchases; owning electronics does not mean I currently want streaming or voice assistant devices.",
    "The speakers, speaker brackets, drawing tablet and label tape assume projects or equipment needs that my history does not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad interest in electronics as a reason to suggest unrelated electronic devices.",
    "A shared connection such as USB or display cabling seems to count too heavily without checking whether the item solves a new need for me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases suggest specific connection tasks: adding ports, connecting a display and getting network access. The practical purpose matters more to me than simply being an electronic accessory.",
    "I interact infrequently and need a concrete reason to buy. A past DVI cable purchase does not establish an HDMI need, and owning USB accessories does not establish a need for more storage."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in practical computer accessories but extend it to devices and projects I have no current reason to pursue."
}
